.SH NAME
git-work-flow - List the flows


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgit-work flow [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
List the flows: their names, descriptions and arguments.

.PP
A flow is one Starlark function stored in refs/work-flows. Its name is the
flow's name, its docstring the description and its parameters the arguments
\fBgit work flow run\fR takes.

.PP
--format text prints one line per flow, the name and its description.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-f\fP, \fB--format\fP="json"
	Select the output formatting style. Valid values are [json,text]

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for flow


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBgit-work(1)\fP, \fBgit-work-flow-archive(1)\fP, \fBgit-work-flow-export(1)\fP, \fBgit-work-flow-import(1)\fP, \fBgit-work-flow-log(1)\fP, \fBgit-work-flow-rm(1)\fP, \fBgit-work-flow-run(1)\fP
